From 403d2133af004f08b4051c887c7b1035efe8982a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:44:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gateway): keep the loop alive while restoring local
 sessions

Startup recovery read every local-policy receipt on the event loop, one
SQLite query per receipt. With about 15k open receipts that missed the
loop-liveness probes and the watchdog exited 75. Receipt and admission
reads are now one query per chunk, and the startup and hot-serve passes
yield between batches so probes are answered. Callers still await
recovery before webhook finalization, native recovery, and ready.

Co-authored-by: Aurora Capital <auroracapital@users.noreply.github.com>
